# TECEnable is deliberately NOT saved here, and must not be added.
#
# The record is PINI=YES with a default of Disable, so every boot writes the TEC
# OFF -- the safe state, and the only state software can justify, since nothing
# here can see the coolant loop (see the HAZARD note in axisSXR40.template).
# Autosaving it would invert that: a session that left the TEC enabled would
# silently re-enable it at the next boot, unattended, with no confirmation that
# water is flowing. The manual states a water failure can damage the sensor.
# Leave it out.

file "ADBase_settings.req", P=$(P), R=$(R)
